      the player can''t jump, check if they''re grounded.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"66af41e6-5c38-4c38-a27b-889ab05fbed7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4427.0,"yMin":-270.0,"xMax":-4289.0,"yMax":-177.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is pressing Jump and they haven''t used all their jumps...","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"33222291-ee51-4967-97e4-bbfecbb0635e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2868.0,"yMin":157.0,"xMax":-2519.667,"yMax":251.0},"title":"Drag","body":"Calculates
      drag.\nThe formula is velocity / ( 1 + Drag ), with a delta time because Unity
      stores everything in m/s not timestep. Y drag never worked out properly, so
      it is disconnected.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"474c5565-6804-4b2d-8e90-dbf8b51c71d4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5719.0,"yMin":-19.0,"xMax":-5492.667,"yMax":88.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is giving an input, store the direction of that input. 1 is right
      and -1 is left, respective to the camera. If the player is not giving an input,
      set it to 0.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"48b5968f-e3d3-4bdb-b0b1-261afe5e9ba9","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4323.333,"yMin":2331.0,"xMax":-4131.0,"yMax":2441.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"If the box finds nothing, the player is not grounded. It is
      still called GravityGrounded from an older version of the jump system.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"be2bcd56-207e-466f-abbe-24ae8351dcbb","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4305.0,"yMin":1296.0,"xMax":-4148.0,"yMax":1361.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Move
      the player with that calculated force.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"cbe3a90b-dc1e-4da6-83c7-1cf2bc14b022","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3436.0,"yMin":-114.0,"xMax":-3336.0,"yMax":-24.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is grounded, don''t move downwards.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"e6ef0479-c3b9-4c19-a9a5-8272e6017139","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6419.0,"yMin":-723.0,"xMax":-6232.0,"yMax":-641.0},"title":"Input
      Scale","body":"Scale the player input with respect to physics times and acceleration
      speed.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"8795115f-c03d-4684-bf27-4e1b8d1a08f7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3526.0,"yMin":1250.0,"xMax":-3282.333,"yMax":1360.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Run
      a cooldown for the defined amount of time. While it runs, update the cooldown
      percent variable for the indicator. Once it finishes, allow the player to dash
      again.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"2b046fea-6238-4d9e-88ce-befcaf137d75","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3381.0,"yMin":351.0,"xMax":-3190.0,"yMax":432.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is not grounded, accelerate them towards the ground.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"91df67b4-f70a-4dec-b0b7-fb7151e53936","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4110.0,"yMin":1588.0,"xMax":-3972.0,"yMax":1676.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Add
      a count to the number of dashes and turn off the button input press.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"38657199-a64d-4e77-b97b-7f7a3ee42606","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6467.0,"yMin":32.0,"xMax":-6297.0,"yMax":136.0},"title":"Display
      MaxSpeed","body":"This calculates the max speed of the player based on drag
      and acceleration speed. It is \"displayed\" as an object variable.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"7114167e-fbc2-4585-a9bf-7f5a5cc91fb7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4679.0,"yMin":1998.0,"xMax":-4484.0,"yMax":2107.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"This lovely node checks if there is anything within the box
      just defined. The Layer Mask means anything not in that layer will be ignored.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"b0759b95-1179-414c-bd47-3ea7a7dd0c0e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6830.0,"yMin":996.0,"xMax":-6680.0,"yMax":1073.0},"title":"Other
      Inputs","body":"Tells the graph when the player is trying to jump, dash or
      fastfall.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"95b35221-73b6-46f2-aeb9-91ac3ffda104","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7031.0,"yMin":-820.0,"xMax":-6853.0,"yMax":-738.0},"title":"Movement","body":"This
      bit controls gravity, drag, and player walking and jumping.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"88859bb0-6601-40da-9ba7-50d08f832800","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-1558.0,"yMin":-105.0,"xMax":-1423.0,"yMax":-30.0},"title":"Movement","body":"After
      all that, move the player with the calculated speed.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"9e86260b-d9b7-4cbf-9478-cc10c84f82ef","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4488.0,"yMin":-824.0,"xMax":-4213.0,"yMax":-701.0},"title":"Jump
      Height","body":"To make the player jump a consistent height in m no matter
      what the gravity is.\nThe formula is yVelocity = sqrt(JumpHeight x gravity
      x -2), but there''s a delta time in there because Unity measures most things
      in m/s not timestep.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"2a859ead-85a4-4a70-a75d-40e78d630db7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3732.0,"yMin":545.0,"xMax":-3487.333,"yMax":655.0},"title":"Gravity","body":"When
      the player isn''t on the ground, they should accelerate towards it. To do this,
      get the current velocity and the constant gravity, make them into m/timestep,
      and add them up.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"d31392d4-e184-4235-acaf-da82c29901dc","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3788.0,"yMin":149.0,"xMax":-3615.0,"yMax":227.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player wants to fast fall, set their velocity instantly to terminal.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"bb915bd9-4289-4f01-bd6c-3cd1a918b1bf","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4515.0,"yMin":1108.0,"xMax":-4197.0,"yMax":1232.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Calculate
      how far the player will dash by multiplying the distance by direction (positive
      for right, negative for left, 0 goes nowhere). Then add that to the velocity
      in m/timestep. If the player isn''t giving an input or the character isn''t
      moving, dashing consumes a charge but does nothing.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"04830f34-b424-4a5f-aa67-b0cad8b7dae4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6500.0,"yMin":1647.0,"xMax":-6351.0,"yMax":1734.0},"title":"Other
      Inputs","body":"Fastfall is effectively a toggle, it turns off once the player
      hits the ground.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"b20b1bbc-955c-40d5-bd90-b432d886082e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8761.0,"yMin":-561.0,"xMax":-8638.0,"yMax":-461.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"Activate
      all the object variables for consistency across scenes.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"eb80ec44-2936-4296-a9c7-fd7d8d8111c9","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4310.0,"yMin":1902.0,"xMax":-4084.0,"yMax":2016.667},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"If the box finds something, the player is grounded, so stops
      accelerating downwards, turns off the fastfall toggle, and regains all their
      jumps and dashes.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"1534c3c1-4511-40b9-85b8-a540a687e69b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7007.0,"yMin":5157.0,"xMax":-6869.0,"yMax":5239.0},"title":"Dash
      Cooldown","body":"This variable is controlled in the movement script.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"f573e478-acc2-43df-9265-db3590badb80","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7618.0,"yMin":4783.0,"xMax":-7437.0,"yMax":4876.0},"title":"Player
      Display","body":"Get the Canvas that has all the UI elements on it. Hardcoded
      indices are bad practice but I am lazy.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"74adc13d-d37c-47b9-aea6-cd5dd53b8253","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7899.0,"yMin":5031.0,"xMax":-7782.0,"yMax":5124.0},"title":"Health
      Bar","body":"Store the current amount of health as a float from 0-1.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"c13e46a3-f180-49fa-9a13-4dd53d897dc3","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8173.0,"yMin":4358.0,"xMax":-8014.0,"yMax":4454.0},"title":"Hurt","body":"Triggered
      by things that deal damage. Just changes health by the given damage.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"c5411e3b-0936-4e21-a32e-923df96d7f08","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8139.0,"yMin":4765.0,"xMax":-7981.0,"yMax":4859.0},"title":"UI
      Display","body":"Controls the UI elements of the player. Currently, health
      bar and dash cooldown.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"b64987ad-401b-4e97-b4ad-3a6de88d3b48","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3914.0,"yMin":-394.0,"xMax":-3724.0,"yMax":-305.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Make
      the player jump by adding the calculated jump force to Motion, then move the
      character with Motion.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"834ea1f1-48c3-4e15-bc28-a7227ac25f7c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6901.0,"yMin":4807.0,"xMax":-6684.0,"yMax":4887.0},"title":"Dash
      Cooldown","body":"Do the same thing for the dash cooldown indicator, which
      is circular but works the same way.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"bd0af0bd-5395-4f43-aec7-2da502dbdb5f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5038.0,"yMin":2057.0,"xMax":-4883.0,"yMax":2136.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"Get a point that is a bit more than halfway down the player.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"e71c0329-35a1-44c5-80ad-d8bd94b1b079","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5539.0,"yMin":1158.0,"xMax":-5361.333,"yMax":1295.0},"title":"Dash","body":"First,
      check the player can dash. Make sure they are pushing the button, they haven''t
      dashed the maximum number of times, and they aren''t already dashing.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"59c87fab-90d2-45ae-a177-6b4632295162","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7385.0,"yMin":4788.0,"xMax":-7259.0,"yMax":4882.0},"title":"Health
      Bar","body":"Get the child at position 3 (index 2) which is the health bar.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"3f7c22f2-7f11-4a66-8c61-f679a60ce6bb","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2185.0,"yMin":159.0,"xMax":-2031.0,"yMax":223.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Then
      apply drag to the movement input.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"dbc73ccf-db8a-454a-86f0-fe7a98bdc10e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5603.0,"yMin":1894.0,"xMax":-5447.667,"yMax":1969.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"Check if the player is grounded for gravity and jump reasons.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"0a690392-568a-420a-b5ef-e38c3752a10d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6448.0,"yMin":2342.0,"xMax":-6231.667,"yMax":2435.0},"title":"Graveyard","body":"This
      long string is for if I ever want to try making dash defined as a distance
      instead of a force. For now, it is not worth it.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"a08374f4-c50c-4647-b3df-971090c0899b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7204.0,"yMin":4790.0,"xMax":-7031.0,"yMax":4884.0},"title":"Health
      Bar","body":"Set its fill to the percentage calculated earlier. This makes
      only the first x percent visible.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"4b6d24c4-7bac-418e-abbe-80d78cdcdd7f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5274.0,"yMin":-250.0,"xMax":-5085.333,"yMax":-141.0},"title":"Movement","body":"The
      Motion variable is what eventually gets used to move the player. First, it
      is set to the accelerating movement input.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"a94951ba-ecbe-47d5-967a-037061522762","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8446.0,"yMin":3232.0,"xMax":-8295.0,"yMax":3296.0},"title":"Visuals","body":"This
      half controls the UI and animations.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"f08138f1-344e-447d-b196-a8a77e067be7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8415.0,"yMin":3370.0,"xMax":-8201.0,"yMax":3491.0},"title":"Animation
      Direction","body":"A little bit of logic that flips the character around (using
      negative scale) and stores the current facing direction. Does it twice for
      now, once for the nice Camille and once for the stick.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"a13ca175-0663-4ff2-9233-6efca5b8dca2","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2558.0,"yMin":-264.0,"xMax":-2351.0,"yMax":-160.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Create
      the illusion of terminal velocity by clamping y velocity to a negative limit.
      The player can go up as fast as they want.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"9959c1a7-811f-460c-a142-6c00ba95de82","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5261.0,"yMin":-1322.0,"xMax":-5061.0,"yMax":-1230.0},"title":"Z-Lock","body":"Stop
      the player from falling off the front or back of the map by constantly setting
      its Z position to 0, the centre of the world.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"c13976e4-772e-45cc-8886-b21e34101c69","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5541.0,"yMin":-745.0,"xMax":-5351.0,"yMax":-678.0},"title":"Input
      Scale","body":"Add the current velocity in units/timestep to accelerate.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"1e93d8ec-48de-4e41-9571-e54275bd4663","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4920.0,"yMin":3426.0,"xMax":-4757.0,"yMax":3545.0},"title":"Attack
      Animations","body":"This system is very temporary. It only animates, it doesn''t
      do any attacking. If it makes it into a commit, don''t touch it.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"c88670b4-dd92-404f-a2ac-60dfe3f04837","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6313.0,"yMin":3917.0,"xMax":-6182.0,"yMax":3994.0},"title":"Moving","body":"Makes
      the stick run relative to movement speed.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"3dee5e80-d03d-410e-a211-578162501c4a","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5717.0,"yMin":3951.0,"xMax":-5514.0,"yMax":4042.0},"title":"Moving","body":"If
      the player is moving, tell the animator that. The animator multiplies the animation
      speed by this value.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"64128d06-def1-4d34-85da-63a4b3cc3687","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5343.0,"yMin":3943.0,"xMax":-5128.0,"yMax":4048.0},"title":"Moving","body":"Tell
      the animator which way the player is moving. The animator doesn''t actually
      care which way they are moving, it just cares whether they are or not.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"b27d58c0-7ee0-4893-889a-5edfcad28ab4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5055.0,"yMin":4214.0,"xMax":-4868.0,"yMax":4307.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"Make
      sure the graph variable for if we are animating attacks is the same as the
      animator one.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"f3b46b49-a264-471f-a043-2f0de9545626","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4804.0,"yMin":4177.0,"xMax":-4614.0,"yMax":4342.667},"title":"Attacking","body":"If
      we are not currently animating an attack, check if any attack inputs are pressed.
      This system is bad and will be improved later when I add actual combat. These
      systems are also basically identical, so I will only comment the top one.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"a45df6b3-b856-4cf3-be6f-decde6a613b0","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4311.0,"yMin":3988.0,"xMax":-4169.0,"yMax":4065.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"If
      the animator is turned off (if we are jumping) turn it on.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"c7ea0431-03ee-4ef2-b2f4-3f71c4df431d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4031.667,"yMin":3579.333,"xMax":-3897.0,"yMax":3688.667},"title":"Attacking","body":"Get
      inputs. They are toggles at the moment. Attack queuing coming... eventually.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"2ae42d19-1444-4a43-a143-b76e80859f1b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4018.0,"yMin":3938.0,"xMax":-3918.0,"yMax":4041.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"Tell
      the animator to play the respective animation.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"38ea13f0-09fb-4c27-80ad-fa80c8b0e6de","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3652.0,"yMin":3949.0,"xMax":-3480.0,"yMax":4037.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"Tell
      the graph (and by extension, the animator) we are animating, and turn off the
      input.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"5b4f422a-50ea-44be-8f3a-fe87919eb03d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3413.0,"yMin":4196.0,"xMax":-3302.0,"yMax":4273.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"Wait
      until the animation is finished.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"baae3409-5dab-4990-8233-d9a1293f429c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3193.0,"yMin":4185.0,"xMax":-2993.0,"yMax":4288.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"Tell
      the graph and the animator that we are finished, so the animator returns to
      its correct state and the graph allows more animation.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"9e9daaa6-f2c9-4fa3-9959-3b64befd74bc","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3431.0,"yMin":4904.0,"xMax":-3229.0,"yMax":5038.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"This
      bit of maths is because the proj attack animation is shorter than the others,
      so I made it play slower, but I couldn''t work out how to pull the speed from
      the animation controller so it is hardcoded.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"72d2d59d-ac56-4e55-9600-7542ef2ca75f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5418.0,"yMin":4965.0,"xMax":-5296.0,"yMax":5060.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Makes
      the sprite change how it looks when it jumps.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"c3d63f0f-7aec-4f04-8c58-33da45c7725c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5148.0,"yMin":5154.0,"xMax":-5042.0,"yMax":5233.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"If
      the player''s y velocity is positive...","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"97f789f9-8b37-4efa-a45a-24c87ca7ece5","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4419.0,"yMin":5162.0,"xMax":-4313.0,"yMax":5241.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"If
      the player''s y velocity is negative...","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"41c21d1e-9cfc-494a-ad47-3616ff0b615f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3597.0,"yMin":5205.0,"xMax":-3428.0,"yMax":5296.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Otherwise,
      (if the player is on the ground) turn the animator back on if it isn''t already.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"6fe0b18c-10c2-458b-9aa0-99f1dcd97e74","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6401.0,"yMin":3414.0,"xMax":-6247.667,"yMax":3507.0},"title":"Animations","body":"This
      big flow is for animating the player (or currently the stick), every frame.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"51ade278-49d8-46ca-8397-873fd1af7490","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4865.0,"yMin":5369.0,"xMax":-4498.0,"yMax":5460.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Turn
      off the animator so it isn''t trying to set the sprite, and manually set the
      sprite to the up-jumping one. If we make an animation for jumping and falling,
      this entire system will be redone, but my stolen sprites don''t have air animations.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"a5170fef-38a8-47d7-9878-ded7fe76e196","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4050.0,"yMin":5144.0,"xMax":-3931.0,"yMax":5233.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Do
      the same thing with the down-jumping sprite.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"31c0d722-45e7-4422-8bc7-f4cadc917967","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"}],"$version":"A"}}'
